using './main.bicep'

// =====================================================================
// Per-tenant parameter template — the full deployment parameter set.
//
// Bringing up a new operator-controlled tenant is authoring a parameter
// set, not editing the stack (CAS Cloud Deployment Discipline, Principle 2).
// Copy this file to main.<tenant>.bicepparam, replace every REPLACE-WITH-*
// placeholder with that tenant's value, and select it in the deploy.
//
// Values supplied OUT OF BAND (not parameters in this file):
//   - Subscription id and tenant id — provided at deploy time through the
//     deploy identity's GitHub OIDC federation (the AZURE_SUBSCRIPTION_ID /
//     AZURE_TENANT_ID deployment context), never written here.
//   - Secrets and the wildcard TLS certificate — loaded into Key Vault by
//     deploy/bootstrap/load-key-vault-secrets.sh, never committed.
//   - sageAudience, bffOidcClientId, and mcpClientId — emitted by
//     deploy/bootstrap/entra-app-registrations.sh after it creates the three
//     Entra app registrations; paste the emitted values below.
//   - sharepointSiteId and sharepointDriveId — emitted by
//     deploy/bootstrap/seed-vault-source.sh after it resolves the document
//     library (CAS-ADR-043); paste the emitted values below.
//
// Identity GUIDs and secrets stay out of the repository (code-surface
// discipline); this template carries only placeholders.
// =====================================================================

// --- Deployment coordinates ------------------------------------------
// environmentName and location are illustrative; set them per tenant.
param environmentName = 'prod'
param location = 'eastus2'
param resourceGroupName = 'REPLACE-WITH-RESOURCE-GROUP'
// tags defaults to { project: 'CAS', environment: <environmentName>,
// managedBy: 'bicep' }; override only to add tenant-specific tags.

// --- APIM facade -----------------------------------------------------
// sageAudience is the SAGE resource-server audience (api://<app-id>),
// emitted by the Entra bootstrap script. publisherEmail is the APIM
// administrative contact. apimSku defaults to 'Consumption' (serverless).
// mcpClientId is the pre-provisioned public MCP client (auth-code + PKCE, no
// secret) the DCR-compatibility facade's /register operation echoes back
// (CAS-ADR-042), emitted by the Entra bootstrap script.
param sageAudience = 'api://REPLACE-WITH-SAGE-APP-ID'
param publisherEmail = 'REPLACE-WITH-OPS-EMAIL'
param mcpClientId = 'REPLACE-WITH-MCP-CLIENT-ID'

// --- Container apps --------------------------------------------------
// imageTag is the immutable {version}-{short-sha} the deploy pins (never
// `latest`). bffOidcClientId is the CAS BFF confidential-client app id,
// emitted by the Entra bootstrap script. abstractionModel defaults to the
// committed hosted Claude model id; override only to pin a different model.
param imageTag = 'REPLACE-WITH-IMAGE-TAG'
param bffOidcClientId = 'REPLACE-WITH-BFF-CLIENT-ID'

// --- Custom domains --------------------------------------------------
// baseDomain is the owned zone the cas/sage hostnames derive from; the
// wildcard certificate *.<baseDomain> (loaded as wildcard-tls) covers both.
// DNS is published manually and provider-agnostically — the exact records
// are emitted by deploy/bootstrap/emit-dns-records.sh.
param baseDomain = 'REPLACE-WITH-OWNED-DOMAIN'

// --- Postgres Entra administrator ------------------------------------
// The Entra principal granted Postgres administrator (the in-VNet bootstrap
// job runs as this principal). postgresAadAdminPrincipalType defaults to
// 'Group'; set it to User or ServicePrincipal if the principal is not a group.
param postgresAadAdminObjectId = 'REPLACE-WITH-ADMIN-OBJECT-ID'
param postgresAadAdminPrincipalName = 'REPLACE-WITH-ADMIN-PRINCIPAL-NAME'
param postgresAadAdminPrincipalType = 'Group'

// --- Document-store vault source (CAS-ADR-043) -----------------------
// The SharePoint site and document-library drive ids that host the cloud
// vault tree, emitted by the vault-seed bootstrap script after it grants the
// site-scoped permission. vaultSourceRootPath defaults to 'vaults'.
param sharepointSiteId = 'REPLACE-WITH-SHAREPOINT-SITE-ID'
param sharepointDriveId = 'REPLACE-WITH-SHAREPOINT-DRIVE-ID'
// vaultSourceRootPath defaults to 'vaults'; override only if the vault tree
// is rooted at a different library folder.
